00:17:30,958 --> 00:17:35,588
The reversy one's especially dear to my heart, because this is some of my prior work on game trees.

236
00:17:36,352 --> 00:17:44,992
you play the game against the computer, and the computer uses a co-inductive game tree that it builds as needed and prunes the tree according to the difficulty level.

237
00:17:45,326 --> 00:17:53,892
in the paper, I talk about writing functions that build a game tree in a sound and complete way, and that is game state is in the game tree if and only if it's a valid move in the game.

238
00:17:54,192 --> 00:17:56,672
So this game's actually using that development.

239
00:17:57,774 --> 00:18:01,540
