00:35:10,672 --> 00:35:15,492
Because so as you know, we had some previous work on F star to C and lots of verified deployments.

441
00:35:15,950 --> 00:35:28,272
And our experience was that even when spending lots of time on generating readable human-looking code, product teams often had unhappiness because it wasn't their code base and were reluctant to integrate.

442
00:35:28,352 --> 00:35:33,412
And typically the last argument was that code was not just verified, but also more performance.

